# PCLN context

Predictive Coding Language Model: Transformer encoder, PCN refinement blocks, memory, decoder.

## Vision

Text-to-text LM with belief refinement, explicit memory, and sparse modular structure — alternative to standard dense LLMs at research scale.

## Entry points

- Training: `scripts/train_full.py`
- Chat: `scripts/chat.py`
- Benchmarks: `scripts/run_benchmarks.py`, `scripts/analyze_benchmarks.py`
- Tests: `pytest tests/`

## Environment

- Python 3.10+
- PyTorch installed separately (CPU or CUDA) — see `docs/SETUP.md`
- Activate `PCLN/.venv` before running scripts

## Phase status

- Phases 1–3: complete
- Phase 4: code complete; prior benchmark numbers invalidated (char-level + exp4 bugs fixed Aug 2026)
- Phase 5: scaling and publication — pending GPU benchmark rerun

## GPU work

Human checklist: `docs/GPU_NEXT_STEPS.md`. Run full benchmarks on NVIDIA GPU only.

## Architecture flags

- `--use-char-level` works with `--dataset wikitext2` and `--data-file`
- `--use-dynamic-neurons` and `--use-sparse-moe` combine as sequential PCN blocks
- Checkpoints must include `vocab_mappings` for chat
- Data loaders return `(DataLoader, vocab_size, vocab_mappings)`
